# Translations

Player-facing text lives in `ForeverExercise/Locales/enUS.lua`. Exercise name, flavor, and steps also stay in `ForeverExercise/Exercises.lua`. At load, `ns.locales.<code>.exercises[id]` replaces those three fields. `enGB` uses the English table. There is no `enGB` file.

When you add or change any player-facing string:

1. Edit the English first: `enUS.lua`, and `Exercises.lua` when the string is an exercise name, flavor, or step.
2. Update every other locale file: `deDE`, `frFR`, `esES`, `esMX`, `itIT`, `ptBR`, `ruRU`, `koKR`, `zhCN`, `zhTW`. A new settings row is a new key in those tables, passed through `ns.L` when the category is registered.
3. If the addon title or notes changed, update `## Title-<code>:` and `## Notes-<code>:` in `ForeverExercise/ForeverExercise.toc` too.
4. Keep the same `%d` and `%s` tokens in the same order. Do not translate `/fex`, `/exercise`, or `options`.
5. Translate with one agent per language. Then one review agent per language, given `enUS.lua` as the original, fixes wrong meaning, leftover English, missing keys, and broken format tokens.
6. Run `node browser/check.js` before finishing. It checks that every locale has the same keys and format tokens. It does not judge the wording.

The dev panel in `browser/index.html` stays English. The language dropdown is only for looking at the popup.
